---
// The Harvard Alumni in Tech H lockup, as inline SVG.
//
// WHAT THE GEOMETRY MEANS. One unit governs the whole mark: the stem width, 47.
// The overline bar is 47 tall, the gap beneath it is 47, and the crossbar
// joining the two stems is 47. That is why the proportions hold at any size and
// why the gap must NOT be closed: the white space between the bar and the
// crossbar is the T, and the T in the negative space is the point of the mark.
//
// Four rectangles, in path order: the overline bar across the top, the left
// stem, the right stem, and the crossbar between them.
//
// CAVEAT worth carrying forward: this geometry was MEASURED off a raster in
// `HIT_BrandGuidelines.pdf`, not traced from vector artwork. It is faithful
// enough to render crisply at every size the site uses, but if the original
// vector ever turns up, re-check it against this path before trusting it for
// print. See `docs/launch-decisions-2026-09-16.md`, "Brand mark".
//
// The mark carries NO colour of its own — it fills with `currentColor`, so one
// definition serves crimson-on-white in the header and white-on-crimson
// wherever a dark ground appears later. The caller sets `color` and the size.
//
// `public/favicon.svg` holds a SECOND copy of this same path, because an
// external favicon file cannot import anything. `src/lib/siteIcons.test.ts`
// asserts the two `d` attributes match, so the drift shows up in a test run
// rather than on a tab strip.
interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className } = Astro.props as Props;
---

<svg
  class={className}
  viewBox="0 0 145 269"
  fill="currentColor"
  role="img"
  aria-label="Harvard Alumni in Tech"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <path d="M0 0h145v47H0z M0 94h46v175H0z M99 94h46v175H99z M46 167h53v47H46z" />
</svg>

<style>
  /* The sizing lives HERE, not in the caller, because Astro's scoped styles do
     not cross a component boundary: a `.brand-mark` rule written in
     BaseLayout's style block never matches this <svg>, since the scope
     attribute is only stamped on elements in that file's own template. The
     first cut of this component did exactly that, and the mark rendered at no
     height at all — present in the DOM, invisible on the page.

     Height is a custom property so a caller can resize it without reaching
     inside; `width: auto` then follows the viewBox aspect. Colour is
     deliberately NOT set: the path fills with `currentColor`, so the mark takes
     whatever `color` it inherits from the link or section around it. */
  svg {
    display: block;
    height: var(--brand-mark-height, 26px);
    width: auto;
  }
</style>
